                <pb facs="ve_d32-1" n="1" xml:id="ve_d32-1"/>

                <head>VE–32. Telegram from the Ambassador in the Dominican Republic (Farland) to the
                    Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="ve_d32-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Ciudad Trujillo</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-08-25T16:00:00-05:00">August 25, 1959, 4
                            p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. Reputable confidential source has advised that Luis Chafardet Urbina, former
                    Perez Jimenez Ambassador to Dominican Republic and who for last 18 months has
                    resided Spain, has returned Ciudad Trujillo. Presence Chafardet here possibly
                    presages (1) return Perez Jiminez to Dominican Republic to avoid extradition or
                    following deportation by INS; or, (2) Chafardet
                    may be offering his services for propaganda or other type campaign against
                    Venezuela or Betancourt personally. If
                    aforementioned assumption (1) correct Embassy suggests efforts be <pb
                        facs="1366" n="1278" type="typeset" xml:id="pg1278"/> made prevent Perez
                    Jimenez from returning Dominican Republic as his presence here would undoubtedly
                    contribute unresolved Caribbean tensions. While it would obviously be preferable
                    if Perez Jimenez were away from western hemisphere, this choice may not be
                    available. Choice may be U.S. or Dominican Republic and of these alternative
                    evils Embassy submits that peace in Caribbean somewhat more favored by his
                    remaining in U.S.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Farland</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
